# Newspaper digest — no invention

Applies to `newspaper-page-digest`, `daily-local-coastal-top5`, `daily-local-top`, and `coastal-katte-top5`.

## Incident context

Oct 2026: News Trail (image-only PDFs) produced **fabricated** PageDigests and Top 5 for 15 & 17 Oct when text extraction was empty. See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/incidents/2026-10-18-nt-fabricated-digests.md`.

## Permanent rules

1. **Never invent, infer, or fill in** a story, number, name, quote, date, or weekday. Every digest item must come from text you actually read: PDF text layer, or OCR/vision on the rendered page image.
2. If a PDF page has **no or too little text**, render to image and read with OCR/vision. If still unreadable, write **"page unreadable"** for that page. **Never fill it in.**
3. Each **Top 5 citation** (`paper` + `page`) must be checked against that **page image** before publish (**Gate A** and **Gate B**). Mandatory and blocking for **every paper** (DH, Hindu, NT), **every day**.
4. **Compute weekdays from the date.** Never guess them.
5. If **any gate fails**, do **not** merge or deploy. Report the failure instead.
6. **Log each day's verification evidence** (page image checked, headline seen) in the **PR description**.

## Gates (mandatory)

- **Gate A:** After each paper's PageDigest — `.cursor/skills/daily-local-coastal-top5/references/page-image-verification-gate.md`
- **Gate B:** Before commit/merge/deploy on every Local + Coastal Top 5 citation — same reference.

News Trail / scan PDFs: vision on page images only; check every page when practical.
